  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62467,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 106,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours are typically localized near the rete ovarii.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:32:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62468,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 106,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Rete cysts (cystadenomas) are typically encountered in postmenopausal women, who may present with pelvic/abdominal discomfort or signs of virilization due to elevated serum levels of testosterone {21139896; 3804558}. Rete adenomas are typically incidental findings in perimenopausal or postmenopausal women {9416702; 2852648}. The rete adenocarcinoma reported occurred in a 52-year-old woman who presented with abdominal swelling and discomfort {2852648}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:32:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62469,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 106,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "<p>These lesions are very rare, without sufficient data on incidence, cystadenoma being most common {2852648}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-23T15:57:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
