        "chapterId": 106,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:32:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62472,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 106,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "<p>Rete cysts are typically hilar and unilateral but may be bilateral. They range in size (mean: 9&nbsp;cm) and may be unilocular or multilocular, with thin walls, smooth lining, and clear fluid {2852648; 15991159}. Rete adenomas may be seen as well-circumscribed white and spongy lesions centred in the ovarian hilus {2852648; 9416702}. The only adenocarcinoma reported formed large bilateral masses with solid and cystic areas {2852648}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-08-06T17:31:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62473,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 106,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>Rete cysts are characterized by irregularly spaced crevices along their inner lining, which displays flat to cuboidal cells with scant eosinophilic to clear (uncommon) cytoplasm and minimal nuclear stratification. Cytological atypia and mitoses are rare or absent {2852648; 9416702}. Hilus cells may form a band peripheral to the cyst wall. Rete ovarii can also be seen in the vicinity {3804558}. Rete adenomas are centred in the ovarian hilus; they are well circumscribed and composed of closely packed small elongated to round and dilated tubules, some with focal, variably complex intraluminal papillae. The lining cells are cuboidal to slightly columnar, with scant eosinophilic to pale cytoplasm, typically lacking cytological atypia and mitotic activity. They may contain Leydig/luteinized cells within the scant intervening stroma {2852648; 9416702}. The reported rete carcinoma was characterized by branching tubules, cysts, papillae, and solid growth with cytological atypia and mitotic activity {2852648}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-23T15:58:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62474,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 106,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:32:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
